# The vendored parser tarballs are third-party archives. Declaring them keeps git
# from ever treating them as text, and it is the declaration `scripts/check-no-emdash.sh`
# partitions on: a compressed stream can hold the em dash's UTF-8 bytes by coincidence
# (`vendor/cosyte-hl7-0.0.0.tgz` does), and there is no edit that removes a byte from
# someone else's DEFLATE stream.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT A SILENCER. The em-dash gate refuses any `binary` declaration outside
# `vendor/`, so widening the exclusion means editing that script deliberately rather than
# adding a line here. Tracked FILENAMES are scanned whatever this file says.
vendor/*.tgz binary
